One directory, named once, so the ROM scan and archive paths resolve

`GetAppBundlePath` and `GetAppDirectoryPath` both fall through to `"."` on
Prospero because neither `__APPLE__`, `__linux__`, nor `_WIN32` branches
match, and `NON_PORTABLE` is not set.

While a payload really does run from its single directory, returning `"."` causes
every path constructed by `Ship::Context::GetPathRelativeToAppDirectory(...)` to
carry a leading `./` (`./sf64.o2r`, `./starship.o2r`, `./mods`). When passed to the
kernel filesystem calls without normalisation, those relative path segments can fail
resolution.

`OOPS_POSIX_HOME` (/app0) is the canonical mount point for the payload, and
`common/posix/posix.c` resolves paths against the same directory. Returning
`OOPS_POSIX_HOME` directly keeps libultraship path resolution clean and consistent.

